    "created_at": "2016-04-26T13:11:35Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-04-26T13:11:35Z",
    "body": "I don't have a problem with moving it back to HTML or specifying the content attribute (though it only has an effect for `stylesheet` I suppose).\n\nRegarding the use counter...\nhttps://code.google.com/p/chromium/codesearch#search/&q=HTMLLinkElementDisabled&sq=package:chromium&type=cs\nIt seems to me it triggers for pages that set the IDL attribute to true because that adds the content attribute. Pages that use the content attribute in markup or `setAttribute` might be much lower. I didn't find any bug about this in bugzilla.mozilla.org from a quick search.\n",
